# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# The screensaver everybody watched for the corner hit: the Luxel wordmark
# drifting over a starfield and turning off all four walls. The track is a
# closed billiard path (`M` lines, docs/spec/scenes.md "Keyframes") — ten
# wall touches in 21.9 s, each key's ms proportional to the distance from the
# last so the logo keeps one pace, and `sine` easing so it glides into every
# wall and pushes off again. Each key also picks a sprite FRAME, and the
# logo's frames are its tints: it changes colour on every bounce.
# Authored for 64x64 — the box (26x13) travels the whole panel, x 0..38,
# y 0..51; on a 32x32 it is on screen only when the path crosses that corner.
S - Bouncing Logo
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Stars
C sliderWarpPercent 1638400
I @pat/starfield-2d
L sprite 0 8 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Logo
I @spr/luxel-logo
#  ms     x   y   opacity ease frame
M 0       0   8   =       sine 0
M 3600    38  42  =       sine 1
M 4600    28  51  =       sine 2
M 7300    0   26  =       sine 3
M 10100   29  0   =       sine 4
M 10900   38  8   =       sine 5
M 14600   0   42  =       sine 0
M 15500   10  51  =       sine 1
M 18200   38  26  =       sine 2
M 21000   9   0   =       sine 3
M 21900   0   8   =       sine 0
